Known non-deterministic flake (same one already skipped for z3-4.14.1 and
z3-4.16.0.linux/.windows, and z3-5.1.0.linux): z3-5.1.0's response to an
unsupported get-info/set-info key is sometimes a clean "unsupported",
sometimes a garbled raw help-text dump ("; Suppported get-info
parameters: ...") that jSMTLIB can't parse -- the exact shape differs
between runs. A .bad golden (exact-match) can never stay in sync with
genuinely non-deterministic output. Observed on macos-14 (arm64) in CI;
macos-15-x86_64 passed in the same run, so this is scoped to the arm64
architecture specifically rather than the whole macos platform tier,
pending further evidence either way.
